message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "samber/hot: Blazing fast in-memory caching for Go"
abstract: >-
  HOT (Hot Object Tracker) is a feature-complete, high-performance in-memory caching
  library for read-intensive Go applications. It ships nine eviction policies (LRU, LFU,
  TinyLFU, W-TinyLFU, S3FIFO, ARC, 2Q, SIEVE, FIFO) behind a single generic API, plus TTL
  with jitter to prevent cache stampedes, stale-while-revalidate, negative caching, sharding
  for high concurrency, chained loaders with in-flight deduplication, cache warmup, batch
  operations and built-in metrics. Its layered design lets each concern - eviction, thread
  safety, instrumentation, sharding - be composed or replaced independently.
